Orion O6: quiet serial console (kernel command line loglevel=4).

Only kernel messages of level 0-3 (emergency, alert, critical, error) are written to the
115200-baud serial console (console=ttyAMA2). Before, every info message went out over it;
each line keeps interrupts off on the printing CPU for ~10 ms, which made the audio DMA miss
period interrupts (DP audio turned robotic, then silent - see also patch 0013). Lowering
the console log level at runtime made the problem go away on the board.

dmesg, logcat and the pstore log keep everything; an oops or panic still prints in full on
the serial port (the kernel raises the console level for those). Build with
-VerboseConsole (build.ps1) / --verbose-console (build.sh) to leave this patch out and get
the full serial log back, e.g. to chase a hard freeze.

diff --git a/sky1/sky1_orion_o6/BoardConfig.mk b/sky1/sky1_orion_o6/BoardConfig.mk
index 6a9773b..5adc49a 100644
--- a/sky1/sky1_orion_o6/BoardConfig.mk
+++ b/sky1/sky1_orion_o6/BoardConfig.mk
@@ -98,6 +98,13 @@ BOARD_KERNEL_BASE := 0x86000000
 
 BOARD_KERNEL_CMDLINE := init=/init earlycon=pl011,0x40d0000 console=ttyAMA2,115200 firmware_class.path=/vendor/firmware loop.max_part=7 arm64.nosve kasan=off arm64.nomte
 
+# Orion O6 (patch 0014): only errors and worse (log levels 0-3) go to the 115200-baud serial console.
+# Writing each kernel message to it keeps interrupts off on one CPU for ~10 ms per line, long enough for
+# the audio DMA to miss a period interrupt (DP audio turning robotic, then silent). Everything is still
+# in dmesg/logcat, and an oops or panic still prints in full (the kernel raises the level for those).
+# Build with -VerboseConsole / --verbose-console to leave this patch out.
+BOARD_KERNEL_CMDLINE += loglevel=4
+
 ifeq (MINI, $(filter MINI,$(TARGET_ROOTFS)))
 BOARD_KERNEL_CMDLINE += force_recovery
 endif
